  "label": "women_at_cafe_with_text_overlay",
  "description": "A scene depicting two women at an outdoor cafe, with the foreground woman looking sternly at the camera while the background woman looks away. The overlaid text reads, \"how dikes look when they're in line paying for their pads.\" The term \"dike\" is a derogatory slur used to demean lesbians, and the meme uses this slur to mock and stereotype lesbians by implying they are frugal or overly concerned with financial matters when purchasing feminine hygiene products. This is a hateful meme because it targets a specific sexual orientation with a pejorative term and frames the behavior of a marginalized group in a negative, mocking light, reinforcing harmful stereotypes and contributing to discrimination against lesbians.",
